<title>USA: Quality Food Centers to buy 25 stores.</title>
<headline>Quality Food Centers to buy 25 stores.</headline>
<dateline>BELLEVUE, Wash 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quality Food Centers Inc said it had signed a letter of intent to buy Keith Uddenberg Inc 's 21 Stock Markets and four Thriftway stores for about $65 million.</p>
<p>Quality Food said it would pay Uddenberg in cash and stock for its stores in Puget Sound in Washington.</p>
<p>It said it expected the transaction to close in early 1997.</p>
<p>Quality Food is the second largest supermarket chain in the Puget Sound region.</p>
